                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you're deciding between a new vs used dry van trailer, you're not alone. It's one of the most common questions for owner-operators and fleet managers looking to grow without unnecessary risk. At the end of the day, this decision comes down to more than price. It's about uptime, long-term costs, and making sure your investment supports your business, not slows it down.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we work with drivers and fleet owners every day who are weighing these exact options. The goal isn't to push one over the other. It's to help you make a decision that keeps your trucks moving and your business profitable.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-understanding-role-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A dry van trailer is one of the most versatile pieces of equipment in the industry. It's designed to haul non-perishable freight safely and efficiently, making it a go-to for industries ranging from retail to manufacturing. Because of that versatility, demand stays high, which is why it's important to choose the right trailer.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "understanding-role"
                  }
                },
